- content_for :title, "How we measure and rank"
- content_for :description, "How StepsFrom measures the walk from every stay to sights, squares and beaches, what the waterfront badges mean and how results are ordered."
- pace = @walks.fetch(:metres_per_minute)

%section.page-header
  .container
    %h1.page-header__title How we measure and rank
    %p.page-header__lead Our results are measurements on the map, not what booking sites say.

.container.prose
  %h2 Where the data comes from
  %p
    Properties, streets, paths, sights, squares, parks, beaches, coastlines and roads come from
    = link_to "OpenStreetMap", "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright", rel: "noopener"
    (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). We do not copy content from booking sites. The map data is refreshed and
    every property measured again each week.

  %h2 Places to stay near
  %p
    We take the sights and monuments that have a Wikipedia or Wikidata entry, museums, named squares, pedestrian
    streets, parks, beaches, stations and markets. We keep every name a place has on the map, so you can search in
    your own language. When you type a search, a language model reads it to find the place you mean; only the text
    you typed is sent to it.

  %h2 How we measure a walk
  %p
    We build the network of streets, footpaths, pedestrian areas and steps that people can walk on, leaving out
    motorways, private roads and ways closed to pedestrians. From every property we find the shortest way along
    that network to each place within #{number_with_delimiter(@walks.fetch(:max_walk_m))} m, starting from the
    nearest street and ending where the path meets the square, park, street or building — never in a straight line.
  %ul
    %li Minutes assume an easy pace of #{(pace * 60 / 1000.0).round(1)} km/h (#{pace} m a minute).
    %li Steps assume #{@walks.fetch(:metres_per_step)} m a step, rounded to tens.
    %li
      A busy road is a primary, secondary or trunk road. Each one the walk crosses — rather than walks along — is
      counted, as are flights of steps.
  %p
    Properties more than #{@walks.fetch(:max_access_m)} m from any mapped street are not measured. A walk is only
    as good as the map: a missing footpath can make it look longer than it is.

  %h2#badges Waterfront badges
  %p
    On the coast we also measure the shortest distance from the property’s outline to the shoreline. If a road or
    railway crosses the straight line between them, the property cannot be “beachfront”, however close it is.
  %dl.badge-legend
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--direct= t("waterfront.categories.direct")
    %dd
      No road or railway in between, and the water is at most #{@config.fetch(:direct_max_m)} m away — or up to
      #{@config.fetch(:direct_beach_max_m)} m across a mapped beach that starts within
      #{@config.fetch(:beach_adjacent_m)} m of the property.
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--near= t("waterfront.categories.near")
    %dd The water is at most #{@config.fetch(:near_max_m)} m away, but something (usually a road) lies in between, or it is just beyond the beachfront limits.
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--walkable= t("waterfront.categories.walkable")
    %dd The water is at most #{@config.fetch(:walkable_max_m)} m away.
  %p
    When a booking site reports a position for the property more than #{@config.fetch(:coordinate_mismatch_m)} m from
    ours, we check it by hand.

  %h2#ranking How results are ordered
  %ul
    %li Near a place you searched for: by the measured walk to it, shortest first.
    %li Near a kind of place, such as a beach: by the walk to the nearest one of that kind.
    %li In a destination without a place: by how many sights are within a #{PropertySearch::NEARBY_MINUTES}-minute walk.
    %li With dates: by the lowest price we have for your dates, then by the walk. Properties without a known price come last.
    %li You can switch between price and walk with “Sort by”.
  %p
    No property can pay to be listed or to rank higher. We earn a commission from booking sites when you book
    through our links (see the
    = succeed ")." do
      = link_to "affiliate disclosure", affiliate_disclosure_path
    Commissions never influence measurements or ordering.

  %h2 Prices
  %p
    Prices come only from official partner programmes of the booking sites. They are cached for a few hours and may
    change; the booking site always shows the final price.
